    <defName>LR_Kontos</defName>
    <label>kontos</label>
    <description>A heavy cavalry lance, nearly four meters long, with a narrow armor-piercing head. The cataphracts of Rome and Persia held it in both hands and drove it home with the full weight of a galloping horse.

The faster the wielder has been moving before the blow, the harder it hits: up to 2.2 times damage after a long gallop. A standing thrust gets no bonus. On foot a running start helps only a little, so it is best used mounted (requires Giddy-Up 2).</description>
